  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I know this has been posted many, many times, though running Vulkan in OpenGL Compatibility Mode (if supported in Unity) will cause minimal disruptions in what is already uploaded. OGL on Vulkan (how Compatibility Mode works) uses the same intermediate format as normal OpenGL 3.0/4.0, but works with it in a more optimized manner.\nPros: \n- Additional ring of compatibility, mainly for the Meta Quest Pro/ Quest 3 rumored to have Vulkan-Only mode and the V44 for the Quest 2 implementing possible Vulkan 1.1 support.\n- Less overhead needed, meaning less lag/stalling on lower end VR systems (near minimum)\n- Is supported in 2019.3 and newer LTS versions of Unity by default\nCons:\n- Slightly more programming overhead, ensuring things remain compatible between the two APIs \n- Some VRChat-standard shaders may need tweaking to support Vulkan properly\n- Some market segments may suffer with lack of Vulkan support, like RX 4xx/GTX9xx cards, Quest 2 (initially), and some Gaming Laptops.\n\nEDIT: Quest 2 has supported Vulkan since Firmware V30, and runs Vulkan 1.2. Unity 2021.5 enabled Vulkan support to be used with it's platform.",
